From: Mano Thanabalan <mano@superlexicon.dev>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 23:37:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?smtc=5Frac=5Fflrc=5Fburst:=20fix=20the=20no-op?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20over-send=20guard=20=E2=80=94=20end=20the=20burst=20instead?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SMTC_MODEM_HAL_PANIC_ON_FAILURE was called with a string literal where
the macro expects a condition, so the over-sent guard never fired: a
burst whose byte counter passed burst_tx_size kept re-filling and
re-airing stale FIFO buffers until the counter caught up — corrupt
trailing packets on air. End the burst via unlock instead; the host
sees the truncation and retries.
---
 smtc_rac_lib/smtc_rac/smtc_rac_flrc_burst.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smtc_rac_lib/smtc_rac/smtc_rac_flrc_burst.c b/smtc_rac_lib/smtc_rac/smtc_rac_flrc_burst.c
index ea99977..b995097 100644
--- a/smtc_rac_lib/smtc_rac/smtc_rac_flrc_burst.c
+++ b/smtc_rac_lib/smtc_rac/smtc_rac_flrc_burst.c
@@ -626,7 +626,13 @@ static void smtc_rac_flrc_post_tx_callback( rp_status_t status )
             else if( rac_config->radio_params.flrc_burst.burst_tx_size <
                      smtc_rac_flrc_tx_fragmented_data.tx_nb_bytes_sent )
             {
-                SMTC_MODEM_HAL_PANIC_ON_FAILURE( "RAC FLRC BURST: sent more bytes than expected" );
+                /* The macro form here was a no-op (string literal where
+                 * a condition belongs): over-sent bursts silently kept
+                 * re-filling the FIFO. End the burst instead — the host
+                 * sees the truncation and retries. */
+                RAC_LOG_ERROR( "RAC FLRC BURST: sent more bytes than expected — ending burst\n" );
+                smtc_rac_unlock_radio_access( rp->radio_task_id );
+                return;
             }
             else
             {
